Hello and welcome. In this section, you will find the full code of our project. 
Since we still got ptsd from Thierry Massart, you'll find a few comments along 
those lines of code to give it a (kind of) clean structure (at least for us). 

The aim of this project is to realise a system that allows us to play the dino 
game(available as long as you don't have a wifi connection on Google Chrome) 
without ever losing. 

In order to achieve this goal, we used two servo motors, two photoresistors,
a keypad, a UART transmitter, two resitors, several cables, two laptops and 
finally, the PSoC 5LP CY8C588LT-LP097 kit. 

We had to link the servo motors to two switches of the PSoC kit as well as to
two buttons of the keypad. A score needed to be implemented, only starting after 
the first jump and going up by 10 points every second. A third switch was 
supposed to reset the score. Every time the servo motors moved (to jump or duck), 
a sound was supposed to come out (specific sound for each action). Two LEDs had to
light up for each jump and two others for each duck. A two-way communication 
between the laptop and the PSoC kit thanks to "Termite" was requested. Finally,  
the obstacles needed to be detected thanks to the photoresistors. 

Enjoy 
